{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-topological-mass-cat-eigenspace","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:topological-mass-cat-eigenspace","kind":"lemma","title":"Eigenspace decomposition of the categorical mass integrand","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-identity","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-descent-eigenspaces"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-topological-mass-cat-eigenspace"],"tags":["descent-involution","frobenius-norm","categorical-trace","mass"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.TopologicalMass.cat_eigenspace_decomposition","text":"topological-mass-cat-eigenspace.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:topological-mass-cat-eigenspace\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha = (\\int_A \\otimes \\mathrm{id}) \\circ \\Delta \\circ \\varrho</code>\nform the categorical mass integrand of a closed cycle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varrho</code>. When\nthe <a href=\"#def:frobenius-pairing\" data-at=\"quantum-universes/quantum-universe\">Frobenius pairing</a> is compatible with the\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">*</code>-involution, the <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-descent\">descent</a> involution <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{\\tau}_n</code> produces an\northogonal decomposition of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code> into descended and transient\ncomponents, giving</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathfrak{m}(\\varrho)^2\n  =\n  \\bigl\\lVert \\mathrm{tr}(\\hat{\\tau}_n(\\alpha)) \\bigr\\rVert^2\n  +\n  \\bigl\\lVert \\mathrm{tr}(\\alpha - \\hat{\\tau}_n(\\alpha)) \\bigr\\rVert^2.</code></pre>\n<p><em>(Orthogonal components add <strong>in quadrature</strong>, not linearly. The\ndescended and transient traces are orthogonal, so the masses combine\nby the Pythagorean law, not additively.)</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-cat-eigenspace.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"11.2.1","page":"b/lem-topological-mass-cat-eigenspace","qa":{"counts":{"pass":93,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":84},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.cat_eigenspace_decomposition","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/cat_eigenspace_decomposition.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
